Q15) Exception Propagation ⭐⭐⭐⭐

***************** Suppose:
main()
   ↓
method1()
   ↓
method2()
   ↓
method3()

***************************If exception occurs in method3() and is not handled there, it moves upward:

method3
   ↓
method2
   ↓
method1
   ↓
main

****************Example:

public class Main {

    static void method3() {
        int x = 10 / 0;
    }

    static void method2() {
        method3();
    }

    static void method1() {
        method2();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        try {
            method1();
        }
        catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Exception handled");
        }
    }
}

***************Output:
Exception handled

***********************Interview answer
Exception propagation is the process in which an unhandled exception moves from the current method to its caller and continues up the call stack until it is handled.

